  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat is the price of a movie ticket on the last Friday? Colby's parents give him $155 each month to spend at the movies.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The information given is not sufficient to determine the ticket price. Knowing that Colby receives **$155 per month** does not tell us how much a ticket costs on the last Friday; we would need the movie schedule, ticket-price chart, or other spending details.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{The ticket price cannot be determined from the given information.}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Colby's parents give him $150 each month to spend at the movies.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Changing the allowance from $155 to $150 still does not provide enough information. To find the price of a movie ticket on the last Friday, we would need additional information, such as a price chart or how much Colby spends on other days.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{The movie-ticket price cannot be determined from the information given.}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Oh, I forgot to mention: Tickets for movies on Fridays and Saturdays cost $11, while tickets on all other days cost $7.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "1. The last Friday is a **Friday**.\n2. Friday movie tickets cost **$11**.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$11}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Tickets for movies on Fridays and Saturdays cost $10, while tickets on all other days cost $7.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "1. The last Friday is a **Friday**.\n2. Friday tickets cost **$10**.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$10}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: the last Friday is a regular Friday, not a holiday or special event.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The last Friday is a regular Friday, so the Friday ticket price applies:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$10}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Here's another detail: Colby buys his ticket at the standard box-office price.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Since Colby buys a standard ticket and the last Friday is a regular Friday, the Friday ticket price applies:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$10}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Thanks, that helps. Now I want to figure out: How many additional movies can Colby see on the last Friday while staying within his monthly movie budget? By the way, here are some relevant details: A tub of popcorn costs $8, and a box of candy costs $2. Colby has already seen 5 movies on Fridays or Saturdays and 8 movies on other days during the month. Colby has already had 2 tubs of popcorn and 4 boxes of candy during the month, and he wants one tub of popcorn and one box of candy on the last Friday.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Colby’s monthly budget is **$150**.\n\n### 1. Calculate what he has already spent\n\n- Friday/Saturday movies:  \n  \\[\n  5 \\times \\$10=\\$50\n  \\]\n\n- Movies on other days:  \n  \\[\n  8 \\times \\$7=\\$56\n  \\]\n\n- Popcorn:  \n  \\[\n  2 \\times \\$8=\\$16\n  \\]\n\n- Candy:  \n  \\[\n  4 \\times \\$2=\\$8\n  \\]\n\nTotal spent so far:\n\n\\[\n50+56+16+8=\\$130\n\\]\n\nMoney remaining:\n\n\\[\n150-130=\\$20\n\\]\n\n### 2. Account for the last Friday’s snacks\n\n- One tub of popcorn: \\$8\n- One box of candy: \\$2\n\n\\[\n8+2=\\$10\n\\]\n\nMoney left for movie tickets:\n\n\\[\n20-10=\\$10\n\\]\n\nEach Friday movie ticket costs \\$10, so:\n\n\\[\n10\\div 10=1\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1\\text{ additional movie}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
